# Architecture Principles

`docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` is the request-path description; this rule is what a
change must keep true.

## 1. Identity

- Every tool call resolves the caller first (`server.CallerFromContext`) and
  fails closed without one. The stdio transport and `OAUTH_ENABLED=false`
  bypass OAuth and are for local development only; the server says so at
  startup.
- The HTTP transports (`sse`, `streamable-http`) sit behind mcp-oauth: token
  validation, discovery (RFC 8414/9728) and forwarded tokens are the library's
  job, not this repo's. Do not add a second authentication path.

## 2. Tools

- Tools live in `internal/tools/`, one file per tool, registered in
  `tools.Register`. Every tool declares its annotations (`readOnlyHint`,
  `destructiveHint`, `idempotentHint`, `openWorldHint`) truthfully and a strict
  input schema; a model decides from them what it may call unattended.
- Tools return one JSON document as text content, encoded for a model
  (RFC 3339 timestamps, no raw binary). Large results are capped by the
  response-cap middleware and every handler runs under the timeout middleware
  (`cmd/serve.go`); do not disable either for a single tool.
- The domain client (`internal/<domain>/`) is an interface with a fake so tool
  tests never reach the upstream.

## 3. Where things live

| Path | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `cmd/` | cobra: `serve` (default), `version`, `self-update` (cosign-verified) |
| `pkg/project/` | build identifiers stamped at link time; the only version source |
| `internal/server/` | config from env, OAuth (mcp-oauth), transport mux, caller context, metrics |
| `internal/tools/` | the MCP tools, argument validation |
| `internal/<domain>/` | the upstream client and its fake |
| `helm/mcp-template/` | chart; `tests/` are helm-unittest suites |

## 4. Testing standards

- Unit tests are deterministic and need no network: the fake client stands in
  for the upstream, the fake release source for GitHub.
- New tool: register it, document it in the README table, cover the argument
  validation and the error path.
- Chart change: `make helm-lint`, `make helm-template`, `make helm-test`; keep
  `values.schema.json` in step with `values.yaml`.

## 5. Generated files are not ours

`.circleci/*`, `Makefile`, `Makefile.gen.*.mk`, `.pre-commit-config.yaml`,
`renovate.json5`, `.nancy-ignore.generated` and every `zz_generated.*` file
come from devctl via the team file in giantswarm/github. Repo-specific build
logic goes to `Makefile.custom.mk`.
